## 7. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: Stream deltas are live-only

Affected surface:

```text
future graph progress observation, replay/restart behavior, durable audit timelines
```

Why it matters:

```text
A subscriber can observe deltas only while attached in the same process. Deltas disappear after process exit and are not returned by retained replay/readback.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep v1 docs/API language as opt-in live-only stream deltas. Define retained/durable stream-delta policy separately.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future eventLogStoreBackend or retained-delta branch must define volume limits, backpressure, cursor semantics, retention, and storage failure policy.
```

### Finding: workerProtocolRouter stream path is touched

Affected surface:

```text
parent-side stream handling, finalText accumulation, pushStream ordering
```

Why it matters:

```text
Mock tests show observer errors are isolated, but real-runtime stream behavior should still be checked before merge readiness.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Run Michael local real-runtime execute-action/nativeWorkerBackend/cancel spot checks before final status.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Real-runtime streaming behavior with actual node-llama-cpp output.
```

### Finding: Synchronous live subscribers can still consume time

Affected surface:

```text
high-volume stream-delta listeners
```

Why it matters:

```text
The existing live event publication model is synchronous. Stream deltas are opt-in to avoid surprising default listeners, but a slow opted-in listener can still add synchronous work.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Keep v1 opt-in and do not add hidden coalescing/drop policy. Add coalescing/sampling/drop diagnostics only in a separate explicit branch.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Whether future graph/control consumers need sampled/coalesced stream observations instead of every normalized chunk.
```

